# ATS Match Criteria & Scoring Rubric

Copy this file to knowledge/ats_criteria.md and edit the weights and hard
constraints to match your priorities. The Scorer reads this verbatim to score a
posting 0–100 against cv.md.

## Scoring philosophy
Reward concrete overlap between the posting's stated requirements and the
candidate's demonstrable experience. Reward evidence, not adjacency. A skill counts
only if it appears in the CV; never infer skills the candidate has not stated.

## Dimensions and weights (sum to 100)
1. Hard requirements match — 35
   Required skills, tools, certifications, degree, and minimum years explicitly
   demanded. Missing a stated *required* item caps this dimension low.
2. Skills / keyword overlap — 25
   Overlap between the posting's named technologies/skills and the CV's.
3. Title & seniority alignment — 15
   Match of role title/seniority to the candidate's level; penalize large
   mismatches in either direction.
4. Domain / industry relevance — 15
   Relevance of the candidate's domain experience to the posting's sector.
5. Nice-to-haves — 10
   Preferred-but-not-required items.

## Hard constraints (deal-breakers) — EDIT THESE
If a posting violates any of these, set the overall score to 0 and name the failed
constraint in the match reasons.
- Location / remote: <e.g. remote-only, or within X of CITY — FILL IN>
- Work authorization / relocation: <FILL IN>
- Minimum compensation: <FILL IN>
